      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles and how their corresponding sides are proportional.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - The original isosceles triangle has side lengths 8 cm, 8 cm, and 10 cm.\n   - The longest side of the original triangle is 10 cm.\n   - The longest side of the similar triangle is 25 cm.\n\n2. **Determine the ratio of the corresponding sides:**\n   Since the triangles are similar, the ratio of the corresponding sides is constant. The ratio of the longest sides (10 cm and 25 cm) is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{25}{10} = 2.5\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the side lengths of the similar triangle:**\n   - The side opposite the 8 cm side in the original triangle will be scaled by 2.5:\n     \\[\n     8 \\times 2.5 = 20 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n   - The side opposite the 8 cm side in the original triangle will be scaled by 2.5:\n     \\[\n     8 \\times 2.5 = 20 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n   - The side opposite the 10 cm side in the original triangle will be scaled by 2.5:\n     \\[\n     10 \\times 2.5 = 25 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the perimeter of the similar triangle:**\n   The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of its side lengths. Therefore, the perimeter of the similar triangle is:\n   \\[\n   20 + 20 + 25 = 65 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of the larger triangle is \\(\\boxed{65}\\) cm.",
